{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005", "score": 0.158, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-005 | Study family SF-APPA-005: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- observed_research_question: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Playoff defenses change scheme within games and between games, especially after the opponent ran a play type heavily.\n- observed_result: Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 523 cells; 440 pairs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-067", "score": 0.125, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-067 | Study family SF-APPS-067: Opponent action T -> your offense T+1 (def-matched 8x8)\n- observed_research_question: Opponent action T -> your offense T+1 (def-matched 8x8)\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: The opponent's previous play type changes your next-possession PPP after matching on defensive team.\n- observed_result: 3/64 FINDING cells survive both matchings: SPOT_UP->TRANSITION ATT=-0.085; POST_UP->TRANSITION -0.083; PNR->DRIVE -0.058 (all also survive +prev_made). PULL_UP->DRIVE dropped as defense-quality confound.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Three cells replicate under def-match, off-match, and prev_made control. Most of 64 are null.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 64 cells tested; 3 FINDING\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPS-067: 'matching primary; sensitivity match on own offense. bh-fdr+placebo+ft-clean. prev_made control. 3/64 finding cells survive bot'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-060"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-014", "score": 0.12, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPM-014 | Study family SF-APPM-014: Play-type label accuracy / distribution audit\n- observed_research_question: Play-type label accuracy / distribution audit\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Inferred play-type labels match benchmark volumes, foul rates, PPP and known team identities.\n- observed_result: Audit overall FAIL: OTHER 20.2% vs <10% target; 40.8% low confidence; DRIVE foul-draw 1.7% vs 14-22% benchmark; most PTs PPP above benchmark band; MIA identity checks fail.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:leakage\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: 'play type labels have systematic issues that undermine adaptation findings'; foul possessions leak into OTHER.\n- observed_verdict: tool_eval_fail"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-039", "score": 0.117, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-039 | Study family SF-CHT-039: Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)\n- observed_research_question: Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Higher AVOID share predicts losing, independent of team quality.\n- observed_result: Game-level rho=-0.19 p=0.008 (inflated n, team-quality confound). Series-level rho=-0.26 p=0.07 (n=50, underpowered; ~80 series needed for p<0.05). Low AVOID-share bin 52.6% vs 25-50% bin 37.0%.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Series n=50 p=0.07; still confounded by team quality (OKC disciplined and good).\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=50 series; stated need ~80 for p<0.05\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: inconclusive"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
